NV308A inline transfers (cellGcmSetInlineTransfer: data words on methods 0x0400..0x1FFC of subchannel 4 or 5) went
word by word through the FIFO walker's general loop (IO translation, the per-word diagnostic checks, the 2D
dispatch) and gcm_2d_method (address resolve, tiling check, write): about 8 % of the FIFO thread in the title demo's
busy part. A run of such words inside one 1 MB IO page, with no per-word diagnostic switched on, now has its
destination worked out once and one tiling check for the whole row; the words are written in order with vm_write32
as before. A tiled destination still goes word by word. GCM2D_RUN=0 turns it off. In J-Stars these runs carry
fragment program words into local memory.

Title demo, CPU at base clock, two drawing threads, on top of 2918: 29.5 and 29.1 flips/s (two runs); drawing
19.2 -> 17.5 ms a frame. One drawing thread: 26.1 -> 28.1 with both. Picture unchanged.
